evidence[1]{path,hash,excerpt,truncated}:
  ".project/done-work.md#orca-engines-range","sha256:cac843d46660866648bb43005793d9e226f0ba65a5c00bc47bd731a13b02660b","## orca-engines-range — shipped 2026-10-16\n\n`integrations.orca.engine` became an npm-style version range (v2.26.0, one day, small-batch): S1 a pure `runtime/semver-range.mts` (no imports; 2480 npm-semver fixture rows, 57 tests, 3 mutants caught), S2 preflight, launch gate and start hook check the range and refuse naming range and found version, S3 config validation with position, a doctor failure on a bad range and a migrator/example default of `>=1.4.224`, S4 `orca-vendors.md` and the changelog. Upgrade note: a bare `engine: \"1.4.224\"` is now an exact pin; use `>=1.4.224` for the old \"this or later\" meaning.\n\nNo-gos held: no network check for the latest Orca, no prerelease or build-metadata support, `engines.node` and `engines.bun` reserved but not checked. Rabbit holes: prerelease tags rejected (Orca ships plain x.y.z); hand-written parser instead of a library, table-tested against fixtures generated once from npm `semver` outside the bundle. Deviations: d1 `config.mts` calls `parseRange` directly so the built-in check always runs (the optional validator hook is unchanged); d2 an invalid range surfaces as `policy-malformed` because config validation runs first, with `engine-range-invalid` kept as defence in depth; d3 no doctor warning for a bare-version pin (documented instead); d4 the test helper engine is now `\">=1.4.224\"`; d5 the migrator got `SAFE_RANGE` so range characters can be written.\n\nAudit, 1 cycle: code, security and test reviewers, independent, planted canary (a raw `appVersion` echo in a scratch copy) caught by all three and refuted against the repo; two should-fix fixed (diagnostics now printable-ASCII with a strict x.y.z found version; 320 more fixture rows and unit tests for `compareVersions`, wildcard ends, boundaries and error positions) and four acknowledged (empty engine handling, duplicated default constant, unreachable `engine-range-invalid` branches, default floor when config is refused). Verify: Node 1560 tests, 1558 pass, 0 fail, 2 skippe",true
